nst the Chairman's own computation or the value routed from other\nagents. Both values must agree before final submission. If they\ndisagree, the discrepancy must be resolved before proceeding.", reason="This task (17 × 23 = 391) demonstrated the value of independent verification: AnswerAgent independently computed the result, providing a cross-check that ensured correctness. Adding this rule to the constitution makes the independent-verification handoff mandatory for all quantitative tasks, preventing submission of unverified numerical results.")
